<span data-as=3D"p">Agent Chat UI can connect to both <a class=3D"link" hre=
f=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/studio#setup-local-lan=
ggraph-server">local</a> and <a class=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langcha=
in.com/oss/python/langchain/deploy">deployed agents</a>.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">After starting Agent Chat UI, you=E2=80=99ll need to co=
nfigure it to connect to your agent:</span>
<ol>
<li><strong>Graph ID</strong>: Enter your graph name (find this under <code=
>graphs</code> in your <code>langgraph.json</code> file)</li>
<li><strong>Deployment URL</strong>: Your LangGraph server=E2=80=99s endpoi=
nt (e.g., <code>http://localhost:2024</code> for local development, or your=
 deployed agent=E2=80=99s URL)</li>
<li><strong>LangSmith API key (optional)</strong>: Add your LangSmith API k=
ey (not required if you=E2=80=99re using a local LangGraph server)</li>
</ol>
<span data-as=3D"p">Once configured, Agent Chat UI will automatically fetch=
 and display any interrupted threads from your agent.</span>
